// =============================================================================
// DataShield on Azure — deployment architecture
// Eraser diagram-as-code.  Paste into https://app.eraser.io
//
// Follows ADR 0001: PostgreSQL for all product data; the two demo databases stay
// containerised because they are props standing in for a customer's own systems.
//
// CONNECTORS
//   >    solid  = runtime traffic
//   -->  dotted = deploy-time / one-shot
// =============================================================================

title DataShield on Azure — Central India

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Edge
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Internet Users [icon: users, color: gray, shape: oval]

Azure Edge [color: blue] {
  Azure Front Door WAF [icon: azure-front-doors]
  Azure Static Web Apps CMS Frontend [icon: azure-static-web-apps]
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Compute — all stateless processes, one Container Apps environment
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Container Apps Environment [color: lightblue] {
  CMS Backend public ingress [icon: azure-container-apps]
  FastAPI Gateway internal only [icon: azure-container-apps]
  Fides Server internal only [icon: azure-container-apps]
  Fides Worker min replicas 1 [icon: azure-container-apps]
  Fides Provisioner job runs once [icon: azure-container-instances]
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Demo-only targets — containers, NOT managed databases (ADR 0001)
// In a real deployment these are the customer's own systems, reached over a
// private endpoint or VPN, and are not ours to host.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Demo DSAR Targets dev only [color: purple] {
  App Postgres container [icon: postgresql, shape: cylinder]
  App Mongo container [icon: mongodb, shape: cylinder]
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Managed data — this is the evidence, so it is managed, HA and backed up
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Managed Data Services [color: green] {
  PostgreSQL Flexible Server 16 [icon: azure-database-postgresql, shape: cylinder]
  Datashield DB tenants users audit [icon: database, shape: cylinder]
  Fides DB engine records [icon: database, shape: cylinder]
  Azure Cache for Redis DSR queue [icon: azure-cache-redis, shape: cylinder]
  Blob Storage DSAR packages [icon: azure-blob-storage]
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Platform
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Platform Services [color: orange] {
  Key Vault JWT and audit HMAC keys [icon: azure-key-vault]
  Entra ID staff SSO and PG auth [icon: azure-active-directory]
  Container Registry [icon: azure-container-registry]
  Log Analytics and App Insights [icon: azure-monitor]
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// RUNTIME TRAFFIC
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Internet Users > Azure Front Door WAF: TLS, HSTS, WAF, rate limit
Azure Front Door WAF > Azure Static Web Apps CMS Frontend: static assets via CDN
Azure Front Door WAF > CMS Backend public ingress: /v1 API

CMS Backend public ingress > PostgreSQL Flexible Server 16: SET LOCAL app.tenant_id, RLS
PostgreSQL Flexible Server 16 > Datashield DB tenants users audit: our product data
PostgreSQL Flexible Server 16 > Fides DB engine records: engine data, same server

CMS Backend public ingress > FastAPI Gateway internal only: PLANNED - DSAR execution
FastAPI Gateway internal only > Fides Server internal only: login, token, POST privacy-request
Fides Server internal only > Azure Cache for Redis DSR queue: queue job, answer 202
Azure Cache for Redis DSR queue > Fides Worker min replicas 1: worker picks it up

// The two arrows that are the product. In production these point at the
// CUSTOMER's databases over a private endpoint, not at our containers.
Fides Worker min replicas 1 > App Postgres container: identity email
Fides Worker min replicas 1 > App Mongo container: identity email

Fides Worker min replicas 1 > Blob Storage DSAR packages: writes access package
Blob Storage DSAR packages > CMS Backend public ingress: presigned download URL

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// PLATFORM AND DEPLOY-TIME
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Key Vault JWT and audit HMAC keys > CMS Backend public ingress: secrets via managed identity
Entra ID staff SSO and PG auth > PostgreSQL Flexible Server 16: token auth, no DB password
Container Registry --> Container Apps Environment: image pull on deploy
Fides Provisioner job runs once --> Fides Server internal only: loads fides-config, exits 0
Container Apps Environment --> Log Analytics and App Insights: structured JSON logs with request id
